## CSS Variable Usage Guidelines

### Priority Order for Styling
1. **CSS Variables (HIGHEST PRIORITY)**: Use existing CSS variables through Tailwind classes when available
2. **Tailwind Utilities**: Use standard Tailwind classes for additional styling
3. **Custom CSS**: Only for complex animations or unique requirements

### CSS Variables Available
From [globals.css](mdc:apps/web/src/app/globals.css):
```css
/* Colors - Use through Tailwind classes */
--color-background, --color-foreground, --color-primary, --color-muted, etc.
/* Example: bg-background, text-foreground, border-primary */

/* Fonts - Applied automatically via CSS variables */
--font-sans: Poppins, sans-serif  /* Default font family */
--font-serif: Poppins, sans-serif
--font-mono: Poppins, sans-serif
/* NO NEED for explicit font classes - Poppins is applied by default */

/* Shadows - Use through Tailwind classes */
--shadow-sm, --shadow-md, --shadow-lg, etc.
/* Example: shadow-sm, shadow-lg */

/* Custom animations */
--animate-dots: dots 1s infinite linear
/* Example: animate-dots for loading states */
```

